<title>NETHERLANDS: Volker Stevin net jumps in first half.</title>
<headline>Volker Stevin net jumps in first half.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     3.20 vs   2.10</p>
<p>    Net/Shr excl one-off gain	  2.40 vs   2.10</p>
<p>    Net profit			     16.1 vs  10.3</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)		  1.12 vs   1.16</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     10.4 vs   9.8</p>
<p>    Income from associates		0.7 vs   1.5</p>
<p>    Financing gain			  0.9 vs   0.9</p>
<p>    Tax					 nil vs   1.9</p>
<p>    Extraordinary gains		   4.1 vs   nil</p>
<p>NOTE - Construction group Koninklijke Volker Stevin NV was expected by analysts to produce a net profit between 8.0 million and 13.7 million guilders.</p>
<p>It said the extraordinary gain related to book profits on the sale of a number of environmental businesses.</p>
<p>The company said its order portfolio on June 30, 1996 amounted to 2.1 billion guilders compared with 1.9 billion at June 30, 1995.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
